    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_74c3f67e474afddca4b386474ac858044439dc660c275704f5faee2081cf1375",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source shows that several superficially different Farey observables factor through the same family S_s: centered quadratic and cubic moments are affine in S_1, while Bernoulli, polylogarithm, non-odd Kubert, Hurwitz-zeta, and selected Clausen averages are scalar multiples or Fourier-coordinate realizations of S_{s-1}. Their RH criteria therefore reuse one Möbius-convolution cancellation channel rather than furnishing independent signals within this construction.",
