    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_d4c3465b4edfde8951c2ea91f3204c7cbaa93cfe8fbf6dca5022c81b342bee51",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source repeatedly separates two jobs in Farey averaging: Möbius or Mertens weights remove the reduced-fraction coprimality constraint, while a chosen function's distribution identity evaluates the resulting unrestricted residue sums. For Kubert functions this yields gcd-weighted arithmetic sums, and for the logarithmic sine function the same architecture terminates in Chebyshev's psi function.",
